@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uic-par-nouns`
IMPORT `uic-par-insuring-clause`
IMPORT `uic-par-exclusions`
IMPORT `uic-par-average-deductible`
IMPORT `uic-par-general-conditions`
IMPORT `uic-par-claim`

-- Tests for the UIC Property All Risks wording. Every expected value was worked out by hand
-- from the WORDING, before the assertion was run; the arithmetic is written beside each group.
-- None was copied from an evaluation. A failing assertion here is a finding about the wording
-- or the encoding, never a value to edit.
--
-- The wording prints no worked example and no table. Its only figures are periods (30 days,
-- three months, two calendar months, twelve months) and the 12 midnight edge; every money
-- figure below is HYPOTHETICAL, chosen to make the arithmetic visible, in VND. The schedule
-- of the test policy is invented: three items, a limit and a deductible.
--
-- The trigger assertions for Exclusion A, one per cause each limb names, were GENERATED by
-- gen_tests.py from the cause lists (the section marked GENERATED below), not typed.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Fixtures — pieces of property`

GIVEN `the kinds`               IS A LIST OF `A kind of property`
      `stated`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances`       IS A LIST OF `A circumstance of the property`
      `the direct cause`        IS A `A cause`
      `the earlier causes`      IS A LIST OF `A cause`
      `the contributing causes` IS A LIST OF `A cause`
      `the earlier loss cause`  IS A MAYBE `A cause`
      `what happened`           IS A `What happened to the property`
      `misdescribed`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alterations`         IS A LIST OF `An alteration under General Condition 8`
GIVETH A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
`a piece` `the kinds` `stated` `the circumstances` `the direct cause` `the earlier causes` `the contributing causes` `the earlier loss cause` `what happened` `misdescribed` `the alterations` MEANS
    `A piece of property lost or damaged` WITH
        `what it is`                                           IS `the kinds`
        `specially stated in the Policy as insured`            IS `stated`
        `its circumstances`                                    IS `the circumstances`
        `the direct cause`                                     IS `the direct cause`
        `the earlier causes in the chain`                      IS `the earlier causes`
        `the other contributing causes`                        IS `the contributing causes`
        `the earlier Loss it directly resulted from, by cause` IS `the earlier loss cause`
        `what happened to it`                                  IS `what happened`
        `affected by a misdescription, misrepresentation or omission` IS `misdescribed`
        `the alterations before the loss`                      IS `the alterations`

`a hundred million of damage` MEANS `damaged, the amount of the damage being` 100_000_000

-- Stock in a closed warehouse at the Insured Premises: of no kind Exclusion B names.
GIVEN c IS A `A cause`
GIVETH A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
`stock damaged directly by` c MEANS
    `a piece` (LIST `property of any other kind`) FALSE EMPTY c EMPTY EMPTY NOTHING `a hundred million of damage` FALSE EMPTY

GIVEN c IS A `A cause`
      e IS A `A cause`
GIVETH A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
`stock damaged by` c `after` e MEANS
    `a piece` (LIST `property of any other kind`) FALSE EMPTY c (LIST e) EMPTY NOTHING `a hundred million of damage` FALSE EMPTY

GIVEN c IS A `A cause`
      e IS A `A cause`
GIVETH A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
`stock damaged by` c `, with` e `contributing` MEANS
    `a piece` (LIST `property of any other kind`) FALSE EMPTY c EMPTY (LIST e) NOTHING `a hundred million of damage` FALSE EMPTY

GIVEN c IS A `A cause`
      s IS A `A circumstance of the property`
GIVETH A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
`stock damaged by` c `, being` s MEANS
    `a piece` (LIST `property of any other kind`) FALSE (LIST s) c EMPTY EMPTY NOTHING `a hundred million of damage` FALSE EMPTY

GIVEN c IS A `A cause`
      e IS A `A cause`
GIVETH A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
`stock damaged by` c `, resulting directly from an earlier Loss by` e MEANS
    `a piece` (LIST `property of any other kind`) FALSE EMPTY c EMPTY EMPTY (JUST e) `a hundred million of damage` FALSE EMPTY

GIVEN k IS A `A kind of property`
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A `A cause`
GIVETH A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
`property of kind` k `, specially stated` b `, damaged by` c MEANS
    `a piece` (LIST k) b EMPTY c EMPTY EMPTY NOTHING `a hundred million of damage` FALSE EMPTY

GIVEN k IS A `A kind of property`
      c IS A `A cause`
      e IS A `A cause`
GIVETH A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
`property of kind` k `damaged by` c `after` e MEANS
    `a piece` (LIST k) FALSE EMPTY c (LIST e) EMPTY NOTHING `a hundred million of damage` FALSE EMPTY

GIVEN k IS A `A kind of property`
      c IS A `A cause`
      e IS A `A cause`
GIVETH A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
`property of kind` k `damaged by` c `, resulting directly from an earlier Loss by` e MEANS
    `a piece` (LIST k) FALSE EMPTY c EMPTY EMPTY (JUST e) `a hundred million of damage` FALSE EMPTY

GIVEN w IS A `A change under General Condition 8`
      b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
`stock burnt after` w `, with consent endorsed` b MEANS
    `a piece` (LIST `property of any other kind`) FALSE EMPTY `fire` EMPTY EMPTY NOTHING `a hundred million of damage` FALSE
        (LIST (`An alteration under General Condition 8` WITH
                   `what changed`                                                     IS w
                   `the Insurer's consent was endorsed on the Policy before the loss` IS b))

`stock burnt, misdescribed` MEANS
    `a piece` (LIST `property of any other kind`) FALSE EMPTY `fire` EMPTY EMPTY NOTHING `a hundred million of damage` TRUE EMPTY

§§ `Fixtures — the policy, the loss, the claim`

`item 1, buildings`              MEANS `An item in the Schedule` WITH `the description of the item` IS "Item 1, buildings",              `the sum insured for the item` IS 10_000_000_000
`item 2, machinery and equipment` MEANS `An item in the Schedule` WITH `the description of the item` IS "Item 2, machinery and equipment", `the sum insured for the item` IS  4_000_000_000
`item 3, stock`                  MEANS `An item in the Schedule` WITH `the description of the item` IS "Item 3, stock",                  `the sum insured for the item` IS  2_000_000_000

GIVEN `the payment`     IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the renewals`    IS A LIST OF `A renewal`
      `the limit`       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the deductible`  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the termination` IS A `A termination of the Policy`
GIVETH A `The Policy`
`a 2026 policy` `the payment` `the renewals` `the limit` `the deductible` `the termination` MEANS
    `The Policy` WITH
        `the first day of the Period of Insurance` IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `the last day of the Period of Insurance`  IS YMD 2026 12 31
        `the date the first premium was paid`      IS `the payment`
        `the renewals`                             IS `the renewals`
        `the items`                                IS LIST `item 1, buildings`, `item 2, machinery and equipment`, `item 3, stock`
        `the limit of liability`                   IS `the limit`
        `the deductible for each loss`             IS `the deductible`
        `the premium for the Period of Insurance`  IS 36_500_000
        `the termination`                          IS `the termination`

-- The ordinary test policy: Period 1 January to 31 December 2026, premium paid 20 December
-- 2025, limit 12 billion, deductible 50 million, premium 36.5 million (100,000 a day).
`the test policy` MEANS
    `a 2026 policy` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 20)) EMPTY (JUST 12_000_000_000) (JUST 50_000_000) `not terminated`

GIVEN `the item`  IS AN `An item in the Schedule`
      `the value` IS A NUMBER
      `the paid`  IS A NUMBER
      `the other` IS AN `Other insurance of the property`
      `the pieces` IS A LIST OF `A piece of property lost or damaged`
GIVETH A `A loss under an item`
`a loss under` `the item` `the value` `the paid` `the other` `the pieces` MEANS
    `A loss under an item` WITH
        `the item`                                                             IS `the item`
        `the value of all the property under the item at the time of the Loss` IS `the value`
        `the amount already paid under the item for earlier losses in the period` IS `the paid`
        `other insurance of the property`                                     IS `the other`
        `the property lost or damaged`                                        IS `the pieces`

GIVEN `the day`   IS A DATE
      `the items` IS A LIST OF `A loss under an item`
      `the paid`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The Loss`
`a Loss on` `the day` `to` `the items` `, after earlier payments of` `the paid` MEANS
    `The Loss` WITH
        `the date of the Loss`       IS `the day`
        `physical`                   IS TRUE
        `accidental`                 IS TRUE
        `sudden`                     IS TRUE
        `unforeseen`                 IS TRUE
        `the losses under each item` IS `the items`
        `the amount already paid for earlier losses in the period` IS `the paid`

-- A Loss on 15 June 2026 to stock: one piece, 100 million of fire damage, the stock worth
-- exactly its sum insured.
GIVEN `the piece` IS A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
GIVETH A `The Loss`
`a June Loss to stock of` `the piece` MEANS
    `a Loss on` (YMD 2026 6 15) `to` (LIST (`a loss under` `item 3, stock` 2_000_000_000 0 `no other insurance` (LIST `the piece`))) `, after earlier payments of` 0

GIVEN `the aware day`          IS A DATE
      `the at-once steps`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delivery`           IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the extension`          IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the fraud`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rejection`          IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the action`             IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the referral`           IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the award`              IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the obstruction`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subrogation breach` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the precautions breach` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deductible insured` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The claim`
`a claim` `the aware day` `the at-once steps` `the delivery` `the extension` `the fraud` `the rejection` `the action` `the referral` `the award` `the obstruction` `the subrogation breach` `the precautions breach` `the deductible insured` MEANS
    `The claim` WITH
        `the date the Insured became aware of the event`                        IS `the aware day`
        `the Insured took steps at once to minimise the loss and recover lost property` IS `the at-once steps`
        `the Insured notified the Insurer in writing at once`                   IS `the at-once steps`
        `theft, suspected theft, or a wilful or malicious act was involved`     IS FALSE
        `the Insured notified the police at once`                               IS FALSE
        `the date the written claim and particulars of other insurances were delivered` IS `the delivery`
        `the date to which the Insurer extended the time in writing`            IS `the extension`
        `the Insured produced the further particulars and the declaration of truth` IS TRUE
        `a claim under the Policy was fraudulent, a false declaration supported one, or fraudulent means were used` IS `the fraud`
        `the date the claim was rejected`                                       IS `the rejection`
        `the date an action was commenced`                                      IS `the action`
        `the date the dispute was referred to arbitration`                      IS `the referral`
        `the date of the arbitration award`                                     IS `the award`
        `the Insured, or anyone for them, failed to comply with the Insurer's requirements under General Condition 10, or obstructed it` IS `the obstruction`
        `the Insured failed to do or permit the acts the Insurer reasonably required to enforce its rights against others` IS `the subrogation breach`
        `the Insured failed to maintain the property or to take reasonable precautions` IS `the precautions breach`
        `the Insured insured the deductible elsewhere`                          IS `the deductible insured`

-- The proper claim on a 15 June 2026 Loss: aware the same day, every step at once, written
-- claim delivered on 1 July (day 16), nothing rejected, no breach.
`the proper claim` MEANS
    `a claim` (YMD 2026 6 15) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 7 1)) NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

